::Properties of a Transaction::
Which of the following are the properties of a transaction?
{
    ~Atomicity, Consistency, Insulation, Durability
    ~Agency, Consistency, Isolation, Durability
    =Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability
    ~Atomicity, Constitution, Isolation, Durability
    ~Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Database
}

::Atomicity::
What is Atomicity?
{
    ~all statements in a transaction are independent and a partial transaction can occur
    ~a transaction should have a single statement.
    ~a transaction can have multiple statements.
    =the concept that ensures either all statements in a transaction are executed or none are executed.
}

::Consistency::
What is Consistency?
{
    ~the database may or may not be consistent after a transaction.
    =the database is consistent before and after the transaction
    ~the database is consistent before the transaction but becomes inconsistent after the transaction.
    ~none of the above 
}

::Isolation::
What is Isolation?
{
    ~Isolation ensures that all the transactions are interrelated.
    =Isolation ensures that all the transactions occur concurrently without leading to any inconsistency in the database.
    ~Isolation ensures that all statements in a single transaction are concurrent
    ~none of the above 
}

::Durability::
What is Durability?
{
    =Durability ensures that the changes made by a successful transaction are permanent even if an unexpected system failure occurs.
    ~Durability means the changes made by a successful transaction can be temporary
    ~Durability ensures that the changes made by a successful transaction are permanent, but if a system failure occurs the data is lost.
    ~none of the above 
}